<title>USA: Hemagen gets rheumatoid test kit FDA okay.</title>
<headline>Hemagen gets rheumatoid test kit FDA okay.</headline>
<dateline>WALTHAM, Mass. 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hemagen Diagnostics Inc said Tuesday that it has obtained U.S. Food and Drug Administration clearance to market a new kit for the quantitative measurement of rheumatoid factor as an aid in the diagnosis of rheumatoid arthritis.</p>
<p>Hemagen said the kit represents the first FDA-cleared product of its Raichem subsidiary since it was acquired in 1996.</p>
</text>
